# Runtime pins for mise, linked to ~/.tool-versions.
#
# Exact versions on purpose — a machine should not silently drift to whatever
# happened to be latest the day someone ran an install. `mise install` (run
# with no args from anywhere under $HOME) reads this file and installs
# exactly these.
#
# mise resolves .tool-versions by walking up from the current directory to
# $HOME and beyond, so this file — sitting at $HOME itself via the symlink —
# acts as the global default for every directory that doesn't have its own.
# A project's own .tool-versions or mise.toml still wins; mise takes the
# nearest one, not this one, whenever both exist.
#
# Canonical mise tool names, not asdf's: `node`/`python`/`go`, never
# `nodejs`/`golang`.
#
# python is the normal (GIL) build. A trailing `t` — 3.14.7t — would instead
# select the free-threaded build; that's a different, opt-in variant, not a
# patch/typo, so don't "fix" it if you see it elsewhere.
node 26.7.0
python 3.14.7
go 1.26.5
bun 1.3.14
pnpm 11.20.0
